  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commercial Digital Services Pilot in Kibabi, DRC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is the development of a working model for digital services livelihoods activities in areas of current or recent conflict. This pilot is established as a result of the partnership fostered through PACE to establish approaches to prevent and reduce the worst forms of child labour in fragile contexts. This pilot is not a continuation of PACE but will build on the collaboration established within it. The initial pilot seeks to test the potential for offering commercial digital services located in Kibabi Computer Centre, Masisi, DRC. The pilot builds on the existing War Child technical skills programme in Kibabi. It seeks to offer training and work opportunities in image annotation and associated AI services for up to 17 participants (annotators).</narrative>
  </description>
